one of the biggest surprises from e3  this year was Mario plus rabbit's  kingdom battle not that it existed mind  you we knew that before thanks to a  bunch of late what was surprising was  the reveal that it was an ex-con like  strategy game for everything Mario and  Rabbids make sure you're subscribed and  you can head the game sport for  everything you need to know about your  Nintendo switch you certainly can but  for now we've had a bit of time with the  Ubisoft innovation of the Mushroom  Kingdom and here's five things we think  you should know  [Music]  mário plus Rabbids is not XCOM light  it's hardcore turn-based strategy let's  get this one out of the way early yes  Mario Puss Roberts plays a lot like XCOM  anyone who's familiar with for axises  tactical turn-based alien invasion  series will feel right at home when they  pick up the switch controller the  parallels are something the devs  anticipated too which led them to  increase the game's difficulty like XCOM  you have to think carefully about team  makeup and how you want to engage  because the titular battles for the  kingdom are not messing around in Mario  Plus Rapids team is made up of three  characters Mario is mandatory and so is  at least one rabbit the third slot can  be filled with whomever you choose be it  rapid Yoshi and his machine gun or  Princess Peach for her area of effect  healing during our preview session we  saw more than one fellow player throw  their hands up in exasperation as they  failed their third try at a particularly  tricky bite you'll need to take cover  plan your movements and rely on team  abilities such as the team jump which  allows a member of your team to be  catapulted across the map if you are to  succeed unlike XCOM members of your team  can attack move and use an ability in  any order without ending your turn and  you won't have to contend with permitir  your weapon choices are varied and  change your combat style you may  remember when Ubisoft 1e3 2017 by having  CEO Yves Guillermo and Mario creator  Shigeru Miyamoto pose back-to-back while  holding replica Mario Plus rabbits  blasters on stage at their conference  turns out those blasters are just the  tip of the iceberg when it comes to  banishing those pesky rabbits from the  Mushroom Kingdom  each character can opt to use either  their primary or secondary weapon during  their turn that could include Mario's  blaster and mallet combo or Luigi's  long-range vacuum blaster and robotic  sentry bomb each of these weapons have  different attack and cool-down stats as  well as status effects that you should  take into account before running  headlong into battle for instance  weapons with a honey status effect have  a chance to hold enemies in place for a  turn while the ink status will cancel an  enemy's attacks the bounce effect proved  to be the most valuable but be warned it  can be both a blessing and a curse while  sometimes a successful bounce shot will  send a particularly strong rabbit  bouncing erratically out of bounds for  extra damage there's also a chance that  it will bounce your enemies into a more  advantageous position for that  or your allies into danger similarly  weapons with an area of effects such as  robotic sentry bombs and throwable  explosives have a chance of damaging  your teammates on more than one occasion  my ill-planned sentry robots ant Mario  flying out of bounds to his doom  planning your team makeup and battle  strategy is essential so you've got a  handful of characters with only three  slots to fill a variety of weapons to  choose from and a veritable crap ton of  abilities to assign to whomever you  choose to fill out your party your next  step is making all those work together  to complement one another just like you  would in any other team based strategy  game you can chain together useful  abilities from one character to the next  like super jumps tackles and AoE buffs  to help yourself get a big boost on the  battleground so making sure your team  makeup allows that is essential figure  out whether you're going for speed mass  destruction or staying well out of the  enemy's line of sight you'll then want  to factor in the health of each of your  prospective teammates there are special  skills which could include anything from  healing to Mario and rabbits version of  X comms overwatch which allows your  character to take a shot at a moving  enemy outside of your turn  depending on how you balance your team  you could have a fairly easy time or a  very very hard one also if you elect to  put rabbit peach and her healing skill  in your party try not to have her die  early it does not make for a good time  tactical view is super super useful your  first step is to factor in the kind of  mission you're playing some victory  conditions require you to defeat all the  nasty rabbits on the battlefield while  others just call for you to reach a  certain area of the map with at least  one of your trio still standing it's  trickier than it sounds when you deal  with enemies who can teleport you or  blast you to smithereens if you leave a  teammate out in the open at the  beginning of each encounter you'll have  the opportunity to access the tactical  view this is a super handy feature where  you can view the entire battleground and  find the best route to the end goal by  figuring out where the best cover is  where your foes are spawning and other  environmental factors that might deter  your progress like warp pipes which let  faraway enemies run all the way up to  you in one turn or threatening boozhoo  teleport you all over the damn map when  you were this far from the end zone as  ghosts later in the engagement you'll  more than likely need to contend with  cover that's been demolished  you were standing behind it to the  tactical view also lets you scan foes so  you can discover their attack and  defense attributes as well as their  abilities which should help you decide  on the best way to defeat them my best  advice for getting by in these battles  is to take your time there is no time  limit so your route through any given  map will be as successful as the choices  you make from turn-to-turn because of  all the different abilities there are  also lots of different ways to succeed  and trying out new options and combos  it's pretty fun  co-op is really fun and also incredibly  difficult  unfortunately mario + rabbits doesn't  feature a co-op campaign but it does  have a great local co-op mode instead of  a three character team from the main  game you and your partner will get a two  character team H if you want Princess  Peach to fight alongside her rabid  superfan you can once you've decided on  who's who you can choose the map and  game type and get stuck into  strategizing just like in the campaign  turns can be made in any order and teams  can swap out depending on strategy it's  also a really great way to lose friends  if you're the competitive sort and  aren't 100% agreed on how you're going  to take on your foes from the get-go  overall I've really enjoyed Mario Plus  Rapids Kingston battle I think if you go  in expecting regular Mario antics you're  gonna be really confused and possibly  disappointed but as someone who grew up  playing strategy games I really loved my  time with this one and I really do mean  my time I took a horrific Lea long time  deciding who I wanted to fight with and  how a long time Rabbids found an  apologist I can't wait to see how this  one fares when it's released on August  29 stay tuned the game support for  everything else Mario in Robertson  thanks so much for watching  [Music]
 

